 4. Exclusive: OpenAI takes on Microsoft&#x27;s GitHub 
 
 By Madison Mills 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 OpenAI will acquire Pierre Computer, a developer tools startup whose technology is already embedded in Codex, the company told Axios exclusively.

 Why it matters: OpenAI is joining a slew of companies challenging Microsoft's GitHub as AI agents take on more coding work. The platform has acted as a central repository and nerve center for software development for many years. 

 Zoom out: GitHub has faced a number of reliability issues and outages as AI coding has taken off.

 Its most pressing problem, critics say, is that it was built for humans , but so much software is now written by AI that a new, AI-first GitHub replacement would be better. Friction point: OpenAI and a number of other competitors may be looking to capitalize on the shift.

 Cursor, now owned by Elon Musk's SpaceX, launched GitHub rival Origin in August. Former GitHub CEO Thomas Dohmke, who launched a new coding startup , announced a competing product last month. The bottom line: OpenAI is moving beyond helping developers write code toward controlling more of the infrastructure where that code is stored, reviewed and shipped.

 
 
